            <ArticleTitle>Foods, fads, and fats in under fives.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>203-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Does manipulation of a child's diet in the first five years of life result in a reduced prevalence of coronary artery disease in later life? The findings of a recently published study (Bogalusa) are compared with British recommendations. Suitable modifications of the under fives' diet are suggested.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
